Upstream-PR:     none (K2Go carry patch)
Upstream-Status: not sent upstream (upstream is dropping 32-bit; K2Go keeps it)
Applies-to:      roles/kiwix/defaults/main.yml
Summary:         Pick the kiwix-tools build from the userland arch (dpkg_arch), not the kernel. A 32-bit library on a 64-bit phone reports machine=aarch64 and got the 64-bit build; armhf now maps to armv6 (built for ARMv6 and newer CPUs) and i386 to i586. Same signal as roles/maps (pmtiles).

diff --git a/roles/kiwix/defaults/main.yml b/roles/kiwix/defaults/main.yml
index 1000d2c..1bb033c 100644
--- a/roles/kiwix/defaults/main.yml
+++ b/roles/kiwix/defaults/main.yml
@@ -40,7 +40,13 @@ kiwix_arch_dict:      # 'dpkg --print-architecture' key would be: (to mitigate #
 # CLAIM: 'ansible_machine might be "i686", whereas ansible_architecture on the same host would be "i386"'
 # https://stackoverflow.com/questions/44713880/how-do-i-make-decision-based-on-arch-in-ansible-playbooks/44714226#44714226
 #kiwix_arch: "{{ kiwix_arch_dict[ansible_facts.machine] | default('unsupported') }}"
-kiwix_arch: "{{ kiwix_arch_dict.get(ansible_facts.machine, 'unsupported') }}"
+# K2Go: a 32-bit userland on a 64-bit kernel reports machine=aarch64 (or x86_64), so pick the
+# build from the userland arch (dpkg_arch, set by 0-init), as roles/maps does. armv6 targets
+# ARMv6 and newer CPUs, so it also covers ARMv7-only phones.
+kiwix_dpkg_arch_dict:
+  armhf: armv6
+  i386: i586
+kiwix_arch: "{{ kiwix_dpkg_arch_dict.get(dpkg_arch.stdout | default(''), kiwix_arch_dict.get(ansible_facts.machine, 'unsupported')) }}"
 #kiwix_arch: "{{ kiwix_arch_dict.get(ansible_facts.machine | default('') | lower, 'unsupported') }}"
 
